namespace trion:
    use software

    section "Sources and citations":
        A source declaration means a declaration that names a source and the quotes of the source.
        A quote means an exact sentence of a source.
        A citation means an annotation of a statement that names a source or a quote.
        A local copy means a file that holds the text of a source.

        [EVIDENCE-CITED]
        The trion processor shall report each statement that has no citation.

        [EVIDENCE-QUOTE-EXACT]
        If the number of occurrences of a quote in a local copy is less than 1 or the number of occurrences of the quote in the local copy is greater than 1, then the trion processor shall report the quote.

        [EVIDENCE-COPY-UNCHANGED]
        If the digest of a local copy differs from the digest that the source declaration states, then the trion processor shall report the source.

        The coverage of a source means the share of the local copy that the cited quotes cover.

        [EVIDENCE-COVERAGE]
        The trion processor shall report the coverage of each source that has a local copy.

    section "Evidence is no proof of validity":
        [EVIDENCE-NO-VALIDITY]
        The trion processor shall not report a citation as a proof of validity.

        [EVIDENCE-NO-CONSTRAINT]
        A citation shall add no contract to a specification.
